QuestGuidance.Register("en",287,{
[9153]="70036404\n1\tSpeak with Avon\tSpeak with Avon.\n",
[9154]="70036387\n1\tSpeak to Shempf\tSpeak to Shempf.\n",
[9155]="700329C0\n1\tComplete the riding course upon the tourney field\tSpeak with Seoca at the tourney field directly south of Harwick.\n2\tSpeak to Seoca at the Tourney Field\tSpeak with Seoca to complete your war-steed training.\n",
[9156]="7007177C\n1\tTalk to Khagâmi\tNabatínu has suggested asking Khagâmi at Gadim-ûn about the brass button you found at Kôth Rau.\n2\tTalk to Rhadrog\tKhagâmi recognizes the brass button as one belonging to Tâklu, who was one of her travelling companions when her caravan was attacked. She begs you to rescue the prisoners, hoping that Tâklu is among them. You should talk to Rhadrog in Gadim-ûn for his opinion.\n3\tMeet with Rhadrog outside Kôth Rau\tRhadrog agrees that the prisoners at Kôth Rau should be freed, and also hopes to learn why they are keeping prisoners at all. You should meet Rhadrog outside of Kôth Rau in south-central An Shêru, where you will come up with a plan.\n4\tDefeat Utûgi gaolers to find the keys\tRhadrog speculates that the Utûgi gaolers have the keys to the cages. You should defeat Utûgi gaolers until you find the keys.\n5\tDefeat Utûgi gaolers to find the keys\tRhadrog speculates that the Utûgi gaolers have the keys to the cages. You should defeat Utûgi gaolers until you find the keys.\n6\tFree the prisoners (total: 5)\tYou have gotten the keys from the Utûgi gaolers that will open the cages. You should free the prisoners from their captivity.\n7\tReturn to Rhadrog outside Kôth Rau\tYou have freed many prisoners from their cages at Kôth Rau. You should return to Rhadrog outside of the Ordâkhai stronghold.\n8\tTalk to Khagâmi in Gadim-ûn\tYou have freed many prisoners from their cages at Kôth Rau and returned to Gadim-ûn. You should talk to Khagâmi, who had asked you to rescue them.\n9\tTalk to Tâklu\tYou have freed many prisoners from their cages at Kôth Rau and returned to Gadim-ûn. You should talk to Tâklu, an acquaintance of Khagâmi that you recently rescued.\n10\tTalk to Rhadrog\tYou asked Tâklu what the enemy was doing with the prisoners at Kôth Rau and did not learn much. They were subjected to torture, and the most unfortunate were the people who were sent to Ombátha. You should tell Rhadrog what you learned.\n",
[9157]="700304A4\n1\tFree the stolen horses at Jóshkhin Orda\tA pen of stolen horses can be found in the south-east of the enormous Easterling encampment on the banks of the Anduin. You should free the horses you find.\n2\tA pen of stolen horses can be found in the south-east of the enormous Easterling encampment on the banks of the Anduin. You should free the horses you find.\t\n3\tA pen of stolen horses can be found in the south of the enormous Easterling encampment on the banks of the Anduin. You should free the horses you find.\t\n4\tA pen of stolen horses can be found in the south-west of the enormous Easterling encampment on the banks of the Anduin. You should free the horses you find.\t\n5\tReturn to Guthferth, Sergeant of North-torr\tSergeant Guthferth is at the North-torr, just north of Floodwend. You should return to Sergeant Guthferth.\n",
[9158]="70030401\n1\tExamine the remains of the tree-herd (total: 5)\tStumps of felled trees can be found around the White Hand Orc-encampment. You should bring the Huorn to the stumps of trees so that he can see which of his former companions have been killed by the Orcs.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have examined the remains of the grove felled by the White Hand Orcs in Fangorn. The survivor grieves for his fallen friends, as will Wisewood, the sleeping treeherd of this part of the forest.\n",
[9159]="70019D24\n1\tTalk to Losdirith at the gate of Galadriel's Garden\tLosdirith watches the gate to the garden of Lady Galadriel, south along the path from the pavilion where Demlindeth sings songs of mourning. Demlindeth has asked you to speak words of comfort to Losdirith, who has been acting strangely in the wake of Mithrandir's passing.\n2\tLook for Mithrandir beneath the overhanging canopy\030Travel to Telain Neduil and find the flet where the canopy of leaves intrudes on the platform\tTelain Neduil consists of a series of flets north-west of Galadriel's Garden in Caras Galadhon, and the leaves grow over the edge of one of its flets. Losdirith wants you to stand at the place he saw in his dream, within the canopy of leaves that cover part of a flet in Telain Neduil, and to look for Gandalf.\n3\tTalk to Losdirith at the gate to Galadriel's Garden\tLosdirith is outside the entrance to Galadriel's Garden. Losdirith will want to hear what you saw when you looked through the canopy of leaves at Telain Neduil, even if it is not what he hoped.\n",
[9160]="700078AD\n1\tTalk to Constable Wren\tConstable Wren can be found at the guard-house on the hill east of Combe. Gail wants to find the brigands who stole her dead father's favourite fishing pole and retrieve it. She has sent you to ask Constable Wren for information about the brigands and where they might have taken her stolen goods.\n2\tDeliver the fishing pole to Gail Catchpole\030Collect the fishing pole\tThe main encampment of the Blackwolds is in the Chetwood, north of the guard-house. Constable Wren suggested that the brigand who looted the fishing pole belonging to Gail Catchpole's dead father may be near the watering hole beneath the Blackwold main encampment.\n",
[9161]="700466EB\n1\tTalk to Aragorn\tYou should talk to Aragorn, who can be found at his pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor.\n2\tSpeak with Aragorn\tYou should talk to Aragorn, who can be found at his pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor.\n",
[9162]="7000889E\n1\tDefeat Shadowmaw-wargs (total: 10)\tThe Shadowmaw stalk the Steps of Gram. Lieutenant Octa at the Isendeep Mine asked you to reduce the threat posed by the Shadowmaw-wargs.\n2\tReturn to Lieutenant Octa at the Isendeep Mine\tLieutenant Octa is at the Isendeep Mine. Lieutenant Octa will be pleased to learn that you have succeeded at destroying a good number of the Wargs in the Steps of Gram.\n",
[9163]="70048324\n1\tCollect Tangled Moss (total: 8)\tBlighted Marsh-lurkers can be found throughout the marshlands for the Wastes. Collect Tangled Moss for Arodor.\n2\tDeliver the Tangled Moss to Arodor\tArodor can be found at the Camp of the Host. You have gathered the moss and should now deliver them to Arodor.\n",
[9164]="700001AF\n1\tDefeat Dushkâl\030Defeat trolls in Urugarth (total: 10)\tGertheryg may be found in Urugarth, west of Tármunn Súrsa. Táni asked you to seek out the trolls and their leader and slay them all.\n2\tTalk to Táni\tTáni is at Tármunn Súrsa, east of Urugarth. With the trolls and their leader defeated, it is time to return to Táni.\n",
[9165]="7002C003\n1\tDefeat wild trolls (total: 5)\tTrolls can be found throughout the Brown Lands, in the desolation of the Entwives' gardens, and the Stone-hole, north of Gnarlstump's camp. Gnarlstump has asked you to defeat trolls in the Brown Lands.\n2\tTalk to Gnarlstump in the Brown Lands\tGnarlstump can be found near the desolation of the Entwives' gardens in the Brown Lands. You should return to Gnarlstump with news of your victory against the wild trolls of the Brown Lands.\n",
[9166]="70024C32\n1\tTell Barrett Nowell to move off\030Tell Ted Ives to move off\030Tell Regina Judson to move off\030Tell Jack Judson to move off\030Tell Bill Hyde to move off\tThe beggars can be found in the streets throughout town, and since the Mayor finds them unsightly, Guard Kember has asked you to make them leave. You should remove beggars from the streets about town so that the Festival patrons won't be upset by them.\n2\tReturn to Guard Kember\tGuard Kember is near the gate of Winter-home. You should return to Guard Kember and tell him that the beggars have been successfully moved away from the eyes of the town.\n",
[9167]="70015E47\n1\tTalk to Lengliel at Echad Eregion\030Collect lynx-pelts (total: 10)\tLynx can be found prowling in High Hollin, north-east of Echad Eregion. Lengliel has asked you to collect lynx-pelts for her, so that she can make cloaks for the scouts.\n",
[9168]="7004117D\n1\tDefeat Corsair cutthroats (total: 4)\030Collect supply crates in Tarlang's Crown (total: 6)\tCorsair cutthroats can be found lurking in and around the Corsair encampment in Tarlang's Crown. Melril has asked you to defeat Corsairs before they can sneak into Blackroot Vale and recover more crates stolen from Sardol.\n2\tDeliver the supply crates to Melril in Tarlang's Crown\tMelril can be found at the northern end of Tarlang's Crown in Blackroot Vale. You defeated many of the Corsair cutthroats and recovered several supply crates. You should deliver this news and the crates to Melril.\n",
[9169]="7001A493\n1\tTalk to Adso Haybank at Adso's Camp\tAdso Haybank is at his camp, about half the distance between Bree and the Buckland Gate, eastward along the Great East Road. Trumric Ragwort sent you on to meet Adso Haybank.\n",
[9170]="7006AE18\n1\tGather supplies (total: 8)\tThe Nêpharai have stolen needed supplies from Hulzidâr. Travel south to Harkhaphâr, locate the supplies, and reclaim them.\n2\tTalk to Bâkhadir outside of the camp\tReturn the supplies to Bâkhadir, located just north of Harkhaphâr.\n",
[9171]="70021984\n1\tCollect venison (total: 5)\tDeer can be found among a series of ponds, south of Harndirion and Gronu's camp. Gronu has asked you to hunt the deer that water nearby to help provision his village.\n2\tPlace venison on Gronu's cart\tThe cart lies to the north of Gronu, on the southern shore of the river. Gronu asked you to bring the venison which you collected and place it on the cart his party left behind.\n3\tTalk to Gronu at his camp\tGronu is at his camp to the south of the cart. You should return to Gronu and let him know that the cart has been filled.\n",
[9172]="7004463F\n1\tRemove piles of muck from the cisterns (total: 10)\tPiles of muck can be found within the cisterns. You should remove piles of muck from the cisterns.\n2\tSpeak with Rathon\tRathon can be found outside the cistern entrance on the Fourth Circle of Minas Tirith. You should speak with Rathon.\n",
[9173]="7002609A\n1\tMud the pigs (total: 3)\tThe bucket can be found at the nearby pond. Gerard Deephole asked you to mud the pigs.\n2\tTalk to Gerard Deephole\tGerard Deephole is at the animal pens on the Northcotton Farm. Gerard Deephole will be pleased to hear that the pigs have been mudded.\n",
[9174]="7000839B\n1\tDefeat Muiráthakh\tMuiráthakh, the Silent Judge, holds court deep within the city of Donnvail, through the arch east of Una and her allies. Raghnaid has tasked you and your allies with ending the reign of Muiráthakh.\n2\tTalk to Raghnaid\tRaghnaid is within the city of Donnvail, north-east of Fail-á-Khro. You have defeated Muiráthakh and should bring news of your triumph to Raghnaid.\n",
[9175]="70027175\n1\tCollect Munfaeril's sigil\tWarg-riders and Ox-clan warriors wander the landscape of Carreglyn. Perhaps one of the Warg-riders or Ox-clan warriors came upon the shrine and stole Munfaeril's sigil.\n2\tPlace Munfaeril's sigil on the shrine\tMunfaeril's shrine lies to the north of Barnavon. You should place Munfaeril's sigil upon her shrine and perform the ritual to call upon her aid.\n3\tTalk to Munfaeril at her shrine\tMunfaeril is at her shrine, north of Barnavon. You should speak with Munfaeril through the shrine regarding the evils committed by the brenin of Barnavon.\n4\tLet Munfaeril know when you are ready to depart for Barnavon. You may summon her through the shrine if necessary\tMunfaeril is at her shrine, north of Barnavon. You should speak with Munfaeril when you are ready to depart for Barnavon. This instance is intended to be run solo, but can be run duo as well.\n5\tTalk to Munfaeril at her shrine\tMunfaeril is at her shrine, north of Barnavon. You should return to Munfaeril and tell her of the events at Barnavon.\n",
[9176]="7005C8AD\n1\tDestroy banners of the Dourhands at Mur Shatraug Destroy Iron Crown standards at Mur Shatraug\t\n2\tDestroy banners of the Dourhands at Mur Shatraug (total: 10)\030Destroy Iron Crown standards at Mur Shatraug (total: 8)\tDourhand banners and standards of the Iron Crown can be found at Mur Shatraug. Encamped at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate, the Dourhands loyal to the Iron Crown dutifully guard the pass to Câr Bronach. You should destroy Dourhand banners and standards of the Iron Crown.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have destroyed many banners of the Dourhands and the Iron Crown at Mur Shatraug.\n",
[9177]="7005C8AE\n1\tCollect Dourhand supply-crates at Mur Shatraug\t\n2\tCollect Dourhand supply-crates at Mur Shatraug (total: 10)\tDourhand supply-crates can be found at Mur Shatraug in Câr Bronach. Encamped at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate, the Dourhands loyal to the Iron Crown dutifully guard the pass to Câr Bronach. You should collect Dourhand supply-crates.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have collected many Dourhand supply-crates at Mur Shatraug, depriving those loyal to the Iron Crown of vital resources.\n",
[9178]="7005C8AF\n1\tDefeat Dourhands at Mur Shatraug\t\n2\tDefeat Dourhands at Mur Shatraug (total: 12)\tDourhands can be found at Mur Shatraug in Câr Bronach. Encamped at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate, the Dourhands loyal to the Iron Crown dutifully guard the pass to Câr Bronach. You should defeat Dourhand Dwarves.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have defeated many of the Dourhands loyal to the Iron Crown at Mur Shatraug in Câr Bronach.\n",
[9179]="70009700\n1\tTalk to Glirion\tGlirion makes his camp in a ruin high atop the hills of Men Erain, overlooking the lake. Helechír has sent you to aid Glirion, a Ranger helping to guard the Dúnadan-ruins near Annúminas. He warned you that the roads through the highlands have been mostly lost to time, and it will not be easy to climb to the heights.\n2\tTalk to Helechír\tHelechír is on a little island just off Men Erain. You helped Glirion fight off a band of tomb-robbers and should bring word of your success back to Helechír.\n",
[9180]="7001AACD\n1\tDefeat crebain within the Wild Ruins (total: 16)\tThe Wild Ruins lie to the south of Ost Galadh. Fuirgam has asked you to thin the flocks of crebain that inhabit the Wild Ruins.\n2\tTalk to Fuirgam in Ost Galadh\tFuirgam is at Ost Galadh, north of the Wild Ruins. You should tell Fuirgam that the crebain in the Wild Ruins have been dealt with.\n",
[9181]="70015208\n1\tDestroy mushrooms (total: 10)\tMushrooms can be found around the water's edge to the west of the Rotting Cellar. Thrand thinks destroying the mushrooms will slow the spread of the fungus into the Orc-population.\n2\tReturn to Thrand in Hulwul-nefekh\tThrand is in Hulwul-nefekh in central Water-works. You have destroyed many mushrooms and should now return to Thrand.\n",
[9182]="7000BFC6\n1\tUse Curtamusgan\tCurtamusgan may be found within the Rift of Nûrz Ghâshu. Galasebdir has asked you to bring him a Curtamusgan, so that the scholars at Rivendell might study it and prepare a defence against its poison should Angmar use it as a weapon.\n2\tTalk to Galasebdir\030Collect Curtamusgan\tGalasebdir is at Iorelen's camp. You have found a Curtamusgan and should bring it to Galasebdir at once.\n",
[9183]="70040AFF\n1\tCollect mushrooms (total: 10)\tThe marsh is just north-east of Tadrent. Haelam has tasked you with collecting mushrooms from the marsh.\n2\tLook around for any more mushrooms\tLook around for any more mushrooms.\n3\tCollect the big orange mushroom\tThe big orange mushroom is located in the marsh. Collect the big orange mushroom and be on your guard.\n4\tReturn to Haelam with the mushrooms\tHaelam is in the village of Tadrent. Return to Haelam with the mushrooms.\n",
[9184]="700173D0\n1\tCollect scraps of knowledge (total: 10)\tThe School at Tham Mírdain lies to the east, up a small incline from the northern slopes of Echad Mirobel. Evil threatens to claim the lost knowledge of Eregion, and it falls to you to recover this knowledge before it is truly lost forever. Faellien has asked you to bring any scraps of knowledge you find back to Echad Mirobel.\n",
})
